# Adding and removing tooth issues. The same flows as Dintel's tests/e2e/tooth-issues.spec.ts,
# written in HumanTest so the two can be compared side by side.

TEST "A dentist adds an issue to a healthy tooth, and it is still there after a reload"
GIVEN the demo data is fresh
WHEN the dentist opens tooth 11 of Ayesha
AND the dentist adds a "Caries" issue with "Moderate" severity
AND the dentist marks the "Occlusal (incisal)" surface
AND the dentist saves the issue
THEN the dentist should see "Issue added to tooth 11"
AND tooth 11 should show "Caries"
WHEN the dentist reloads the page
THEN tooth 11 should show "Caries"
AND the page should have no accessibility problems
END


TEST "The issue form explains the clinic rules before saving"
GIVEN the demo data is fresh
WHEN the dentist opens tooth 11 of Ayesha
AND the dentist starts adding an issue
AND the dentist saves the issue
THEN the issue form should say "Choose a condition"
AND the issue form should say "Choose a severity"
AND "Condition" field should be focused
WHEN the dentist chooses "Caries" for Condition
AND the dentist chooses "Mild" for Severity
AND the dentist saves the issue
THEN the issue form should say "Caries needs at least one surface"
AND the page should have no accessibility problems
END


TEST "Removing an issue asks first, then the issue is gone for good"
GIVEN the demo data is fresh
WHEN the dentist opens tooth 31 of Ayesha
AND the dentist removes the "gingivitis" issue
THEN the dentist should see "Remove gingivitis on tooth 31?"
AND the dentist should see "This can't be undone."
AND the page should have no accessibility problems
WHEN the dentist confirms the removal
THEN the dentist should see "Issue removed from tooth 31"
AND "Add issue" button should be focused
WHEN the dentist reloads the page
THEN tooth 31 should have no active issues
END
